break - is used in switch and loops(for/while/do while)
      - used to exit from the loop, when the output gets prints.
eg: 
for(i = 1; i <= 10; i++)
{
if(i == 5)
{
break;
}
printf("%d", i);
}

output: 1 2 3 4

WHY break?
The loop here executes 10 times i.e, the max number of loop executing are 10, in that the loop will end with the help of break when the i value is equals to 5.

PRIME NUMBER - it is divisible by 1 and itself only.






